          "id": "the_six_equipment_points_are_the_complete_set_for_three_sccs",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.1, §6.2 and §6.3's equipment points, all six of them, and the check that there is no seventh.\n\nWHAT IS DECLARED AND WHAT IS READ. Only the six sourceTypeIDs are declared; every SCC below is JOINED out of nrsourceusetype from them, so a mistyped source type moves an SCC and the comparison against MOVESOutput fails on the key set. That leaves one hole a declaration always leaves -- OMISSION -- and `scc_equipmentPointCount` closes it by counting, out of the 1,183-row table and the 62,699-row population table, how many points each SCC really has: one, three, two. A seventh point in the snapshot makes this red; dropping one of ours makes it red as well, from the other side, because the missing point's own count assertion disappears with it.\n\nTHREE SCCs OVER SIX POINTS is the shape the whole widening exists for: 2265007010's three points sum into each of its output rows and 2265007015's two into each of its.",
