        {
          "id": "getind_picks_2002_out_of_62821_rows",
          "description": "§6.0 and §2.1: county 26161 quant 1,512,186 and state 26000 quant 466,969,286, both at surrogateYearID 2002, giving allocFrac 0.0032382986. The year rule matters over the real table in a way it cannot over a transcription -- surrogate 8 carries several years, and taking the largest year rather than the latest AT OR BEFORE 2020, or summing the years instead of selecting one, both give a number of the right order of magnitude.\n\nBINARY32 QUANTITIES: every number this test pins is a floating-point quantity, so it asserts at one binary32 epsilon (2^-23) rather than the model's 1e-12 -- the resolution of the declared element type. The tests that pin a ten-digit key keep the exact default; the precision note in `metadata.description` says why a key must never be compared within a tolerance.",
