        {
          "id": "population_and_geography_meet_at_the_worked_example",
          "description": "§6.1 step 1: round1dp(83.279224) x 0.0032382986 = 0.26975028. This is the number components/exhaust_rollup.esm carries as a parameter default, arrived at here from two tables neither of which contains it. The float32 reference prints 0.269750297, and now that this document is evaluated in float32 it computes 0.26975029706954956 -- the same number, and 7.8e-08 from the binary64 value asserted here, which is the 8th significant figure and one epsilon. The `expected` is deliberately still the binary64 value: it is derivable from the two tables by hand, and it makes this assertion a check on the arithmetic rather than a transcription of the reference's answer.\n\nBINARY32 QUANTITIES: every number this test pins is a floating-point quantity, so it asserts at one binary32 epsilon (2^-23) rather than the model's 1e-12 -- the resolution of the declared element type. The tests that pin a ten-digit key keep the exact default; the precision note in `metadata.description` says why a key must never be compared within a tolerance.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
