              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2260007000.0,
              "coords": {
                "equipment_point_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_temporal_factors_match_the_worked_example",
          "description": "§6.0: monthFraction 0.0833333 out of 46,428 rows, dayFraction 0.166667 out of 210, tpltmp 0.09722238, and adjtime 1/31. The month fraction is NOT 1/12 -- it is within 1e-7 of it and read from the table, and the two are worth telling apart because a lookup that missed would silently fall back to defmth = 1/12 and be right to six figures.\n\nBINARY32 QUANTITIES: every number this test pins is a floating-point quantity, so it asserts at one binary32 epsilon (2^-23) rather than the model's 1e-12 -- the resolution of the declared element type. The tests that pin a ten-digit key keep the exact default; the precision note in `metadata.description` says why a key must never be compared within a tolerance. One epsilon still separates the table's 0.0833333 from the `defmth = 1/12` a missed lookup would deliver: they are 4.0e-07 apart, a factor of 3.3 outside this tolerance.",
          "time_span": {
