        {
          "id": "scrptime_runs_on_the_real_scrappage_curve",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.1 step 2, computed here for the first time rather than carried. Every number in that step now comes out of the snapshot: the 197-row nrscrappagecurve, nrsourceusetype's four activity columns, and the growth series below. What it discriminates:\n\nTHE STEP LOOKUP IS A STEP LOOKUP. Age 2's fraction of life used is 1.1104711, and the default curve's breakpoints straddle it at 1.1106 (73.5%) and 1.1178 (74%) -- find_scrappage_percent takes the last breakpoint AT OR BELOW, so 73.5, and an interpolating lookup would give 73.6. Age 3 is at 2.2209423, past the curve's last breakpoint of 2.0, so it reads the terminal 100.\n\nTHE YEAR-OVER-YEAR FRACTION IS NOT A DIFFERENCE OF CUMULATIVES. Age 3's is 100 x 0.265 / 26.5, the fraction of the survivors at age 2 that go, not 100 - 73.5.\n\n§7.3 IS NOW COMPUTED HERE. The age-3 survival is 5.9604645e-08 and not 0, because this document declares Float32 and 100 x 0.265 / 26.5 is 0.99999994 in binary32 and exactly 1 in binary64. That residue is what carries model year 2018 through thirty fold iterations into four MOVESOutput rows, and until this commit the fixture asserted nothing about it -- it arrived inside a carried constant. The value is asserted at 2^-23 RELATIVE, which on 5.96e-08 is 7e-15 absolute, so the assertion separates it from zero by eight orders of magnitude rather than tolerating either.\n\nBINARY32 QUANTITIES: the percents and nyrlif are exact counts and keep the model's 1e-12; the rest are quantities and carry one binary32 epsilon.",
