        {
          "id": "the_fold_reproduces_the_reference_fractions_exactly_in_float32",
          "description": "agedist.f's thirty-year fold, COMPUTED here rather than carried, against the three real*4 values docs/nonroad-logging-county.md 6.1 step 3 transcribes from the reference. They are reproduced to the last bit: 3.707268476486206 IS binary32's 3.7072685, and 5.888558263222876e-08 IS binary32's 5.8885583e-08. That last one is the whole of 7.3 -- it is the age-3 cohort's grown fraction, it is positive only because the age-3 survival is 5.96e-08 in real*4 where binary64 makes it exactly zero, and it is what decides whether this SCC has three model years or two. So the document's row set is now PRODUCED by the declared element type instead of depending on a constant that was typed in. The tolerance is the model default and stays exact: these are not approximations of the reference values, they are the same binary32 numbers.",
