              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_computed_age_distribution_sums_to_the_growth_ratio",
          "description": "The cross-check on the fold's own answer. It used to keep a CARRIED column honest; the column is computed now, and the check is worth more rather than less, because it closes the loop by a route the fold never touches. The three grown fractions must sum to the cumulative growth G(2020)/G(1990), which this document derives from nrgrowthindex through the pattern finder's ladder and two exact rows of a 50,955-row table -- no scrappage curve, no survivals, no recurrence. 4.6978168 against 4.6978192, agreeing to 5.2e-07, which is four epsilons of the declared element type and is where two float32 fractions summed in float32 should land. The gap is in the FRACTIONS, not in the summing, so it does not tighten with precision.",
