        {
          "id": "the_fold_runs_once_per_equipment_point",
          "description": "agedist.f is called once per equipment point and its answer depends on the point's own base population, so six points means six thirty-year folds and not one broadcast six ways. Points 2 and 3 are the proof: they agree in every input except population (647.2 against 35.8) and their grown fractions differ in the last bits -- 0.2246546745300293 against 0.2246541976928711 -- which a shared fold could not produce and which no tolerance loose enough to be useful could tell from equality. All fourteen values below are the reference's own real*4 numbers to the last bit, so the model default of 1e-12 applies and they are EQUALITIES.\n\nThe totals are the fold's only end-to-end self-check: agedist's residual makes the whole vector sum to totpop/baspop, and that ratio comes out of nrgrowthindex by a different route entirely (`point_cumulativeGrowthRatio` = 4.697819). Six independent thirty-iteration recurrences landing within 5e-07 of one externally derived constant is not something a broken fold does.\n\n§6.3 calls point 4's `nyrlif` 38; it is 39, and 38 is the oldest slot the skip leaves populated. The document computes it and the number below is what scrptime.f produces.",
