        {
          "id": "the_model_year_set_of_2265007010_is_gappy_where_the_residual_went_negative",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.3, and the thing it calls the single most fragile behaviour in the whole chain. The growth indicator for pattern 2176 FALLS between 1999 (1481) and 2000 (1000), so grwfac(1999, 2000) is -0.32478055; agedist.f's residual `mdyrfrc[0] = totpopfrc - frcsum` is not clamped, comes out at or below zero in those years, and prccty.f's skip then drops the cohort. The result is a model-year set with holes in it -- 1991, 2000, 2001, 2002 and 2006-2010 absent from a span that otherwise runs unbroken from 1983 to 2020.\n\nEvery hole below is asserted against its NEIGHBOURS, not on its own, because 'this slot is empty' is satisfied by a chain that computes nothing at all. Slot 11 is empty and slot 10 is not; slot 15 is empty and slot 16 is not; slot 30 (model year 1991) is empty between two populated slots. It depends jointly on the integer truncation of the growth index, on the residual NOT being clamped, and on the skip: fix the clamp and the holes fill in, and the row count goes from 144 to 188.",
