        {
          "id": "the_mix_year_moves_with_the_model_year_on_2265007010",
          "description": "§6.3's third bullet: the 'latest mix year at or before this model year' rule, exercised across a bin that carries eleven distinct mix years (1900, 1996, 1997, 2001-2005, 2011, 2013, 2015) over 29 model years. On 2260007005 the rule is degenerate -- all three cohorts take 2008 -- so until this SCC landed nothing in this document distinguished it from 'take the newest mix' or 'take the oldest'. Here model year 2020 takes 2015, 2014 takes 2013, 2012 takes 2011, and 1996 takes 1996 while 1995 falls through to the 1900 catch-all. Taking the newest would put 2015 on all of them; taking the nearest would put 1996 on 1995.",
