          "id": "the_sixteen_rows_of_worked_example_B_end_to_end",
          "description": "docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §6.2's whole result table, which is the first place in this document where an output row is a SUM OVER EQUIPMENT POINTS. Model year 2020 and 2019 take both of 2265007015's points; 2018 and 2017 take only the hp-9.0 one, because the hp-5.5 point's nyrlif is 3 and its third slot is exactly zero. Getting the union of the two points' model years wrong in either direction changes the row count, and getting the sum wrong changes only the number -- so the key columns are asserted alongside.\n\nThe expected values are the independent float32 reproduction of §6.5, not this chain's own output and not the snapshot's six significant figures. It associates clcems.f's roll-up as the Fortran does, one operation at a time, while this document writes it as one flat product and lets the runtime order it; that is the only difference between the two routes and it is bounded by the arithmetic rather than fitted. The product has eleven factors and is summed over up to three technologies, so about fourteen roundings can differ, at half a binary32 epsilon each: eight epsilons is the bound, and 3.4e-07 -- 2.8 epsilons -- is the largest disagreement measured over all 144 cells.",
